Two gaps against the sync sibling, both visible in `lib/Net/Async/Hetzner/Cloud.pm:49-59`:

1. `_http` builds Net::Async::HTTP without `timeout`, and `configure` (`Cloud.pm:18-25`) accepts only `token`/`base_url` (`user`/`password` for Robot). A stalled connection keeps the Future pending forever; `WWW::Hetzner::LWPIO` defaults to 30 s. A cached `_cloud`/`_robot` also means `configure(token => ...)` after the first request has no effect on what is sent.
2. WWW::Hetzner 0.101 added `WWW::Hetzner::Storage` (Storage Boxes, third API host). There is no `Net::Async::Hetzner::Storage`; `grep -ri storage lib README.md` is empty. `Cloud.pm` and `Robot.pm` are line-for-line copies apart from auth (see `diff`), so a shared base class would make the third client a few lines.

Done when: `timeout` is configurable with a 30 s default, reconfiguring credentials drops the cached sync client, and `Net::Async::Hetzner::Storage` exists on a shared transport base with a mock test like `t/cloud.t`.

